                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3b6d894-88e6-460a-acbe-1a4f3171bc90",
                                                "sense_id": "ba124ec6-1a1e-3dc9-9dea-4157487fc6fe",
                                                "text": "We must fatten the turkey in time for Thanksgiving."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "242b8400-af17-42b8-97ee-23c05b29adcd",
                                                "sense_id": "ba124ec6-1a1e-3dc9-9dea-4157487fc6fe",
                                                "text": "And if the mat[t]er be too little, the vertue of digestion fayleth, and the bodye is dryed, and if the matter and meate be moderate, the meats is well digested, and the bodye fattened, the heart comforted, kinde heate made more, the humors made temperate, & wit made cleere:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "070cd72c-4024-4b40-a3b2-226de7e2f487",
                                                "sense_id": "ba124ec6-1a1e-3dc9-9dea-4157487fc6fe",
                                                "text": "In that classroom full of oily potato-chip-fattened adolescents, she was everyone’s ideal of translucent perfume-advertisement femininity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a91d866-2270-3ff6-a70a-e4118ed0cc3a",
                                        "entry_id": "217b1faa-61b5-3778-a8ad-1b6fd225d0ad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To become fat or fatter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b543a2a5-4561-4123-80df-37e8bd3c20f1",
                                                "sense_id": "0a91d866-2270-3ff6-a70a-e4118ed0cc3a",
                                                "text": "He gradually fattened in the five years after getting married."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7d45de6-5800-4633-85b3-23ef7ef6189b",
                                                "sense_id": "0a91d866-2270-3ff6-a70a-e4118ed0cc3a",
                                                "text": "The Laplanders, possessing a country where corn will not grow, make bread of the inner bark of trees; and Linneus reports, that swine there fatten on that food […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c041da4-4d91-4866-8fa2-40dee128baa3",
                                                "sense_id": "0a91d866-2270-3ff6-a70a-e4118ed0cc3a",
                                                "text": "His soul was fattening and congealing into a gross grease, plunging ever deeper in its dull fear into a sombre threatening dusk […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d017134b-8ac5-430f-a812-33a403a5a234",
                                                "sense_id": "0a91d866-2270-3ff6-a70a-e4118ed0cc3a",
                                                "text": "Mushrooms fatten in the warm September rain."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d1e3cf5f-3dc3-3052-8f66-b181c3ee0260",
                                        "entry_id": "217b1faa-61b5-3778-a8ad-1b6fd225d0ad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make thick or thicker (often something containing paper, especially money)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b750545-e741-44a5-8c34-8147c1602451",
                                                "sense_id": "d1e3cf5f-3dc3-3052-8f66-b181c3ee0260",
                                                "text": "“You horrible old man, you’ve always tried to turn Erik into a slave, to fatten your pocketbook! […]”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc37f2b7-8af8-41a6-bbfa-607725053b61",
                                                "sense_id": "d1e3cf5f-3dc3-3052-8f66-b181c3ee0260",
                                                "text": "[…] stirred by the air / That freshened from the window, these ascended ⁠/ In fattening the prolonged candle-flames, / Flung their smoke into the laquearia, / Stirring the pattern on the coffered ceiling."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04d9a2e8-1f55-4bcc-862b-9e3be7063fb5",
                                                "sense_id": "d1e3cf5f-3dc3-3052-8f66-b181c3ee0260",
                                                "text": "The news spread, about the bastard caterer who was toying with their religious sentiments, trampling on their beliefs, polluting their beings, all for the sake of fattening his miserable wallet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6deba7fd-4cdd-4cfc-8848-0e8daf21fd93",
                                                "sense_id": "d1e3cf5f-3dc3-3052-8f66-b181c3ee0260",
                                                "text": "It was the impotence of the money, and of all the pent-up warlike fancies that had earned it, to do anything but elaborate the wardrobe and fatten the financial portfolios of the owners of Empire Comics that so frustrated and enraged him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f96880bc-aeb9-30c4-9b65-8e243b2449d6",
                                        "entry_id": "217b1faa-61b5-3778-a8ad-1b6fd225d0ad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To become thick or thicker."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15c43ae2-b0af-4ac7-8ec8-7621bf473a05",
                                                "sense_id": "f96880bc-aeb9-30c4-9b65-8e243b2449d6",
                                                "text": "A broad river of white paper rushed constantly up from the cylinder and leaped into a mangling chaos of machinery whence it emerged a second later, cut, printed, folded and stacked, sliding along a board with a hundred others in a fattening sheaf."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b620bbc-7a63-4129-922b-f09ccf096415",
                                                "sense_id": "f96880bc-aeb9-30c4-9b65-8e243b2449d6",
                                                "text": "The pencil-line of light by his feet fattened to a bar. Alan looked around and saw Norris Ridgewick."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9d82e3f5-a1ea-3c61-adf1-c98ff1226b9d",
                                        "entry_id": "217b1faa-61b5-3778-a8ad-1b6fd225d0ad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make (soil) fertile and fruitful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df859beb-2906-4c9f-b419-3e71d0e6e9ac",
                                                "sense_id": "9d82e3f5-a1ea-3c61-adf1-c98ff1226b9d",
                                                "text": "to fatten land"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e63e772-bb9a-47e2-a515-25066a92c7f1",
                                                "sense_id": "9d82e3f5-a1ea-3c61-adf1-c98ff1226b9d",
                                                "text": "1612, Joseph Hall, Contemplations vpon the Principall Passages of the Holie Storie, London: Sa. Macham, Volume 1, Book 4, p. 333,\nAs the riuer of Nilus was to Egypt in steed of heauen to moisten and fatten the earth; so their confidence was more in it then in heauen;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0b96cbf-deb1-40eb-ada8-662e096c3d1c",
                                                "sense_id": "9d82e3f5-a1ea-3c61-adf1-c98ff1226b9d",
                                                "text": "The earth is fattened with our dead;\nShe swallows more and doth not cease:\nTherefore her wine and oil increase\nAnd her sheaves are not numberèd;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "391f6219-928d-3d55-93c3-2285f8535780",
                                        "entry_id": "217b1faa-61b5-3778-a8ad-1b6fd225d0ad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To become fertile and fruitful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6eeaf92-45c9-49d7-a635-9ebcf9e90339",
                                                "sense_id": "391f6219-928d-3d55-93c3-2285f8535780",
                                                "text": "These hostile Fields shall fatten with thy Blood."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
